  "title": "Battery Storage, Hybrid Projects Dominate Renewable Auctions in Q3 2026",
  "summary": "Government agencies issued tenders for 21 GW of renewable energy capacity and auctioned 12 GW across energy storage, hybrid, large-scale solar, wind, manufacturing, green hydrogen, and rooftop solar projects in the third quarter (Q3) of 2026, according to Mercom India’s newly released Q3 and 9M 2026 India Renewable Energy Procurement and Demand Report.Wind projects led auction activity with 3.2 GW, followed by battery energy storage at 2.8 GW, hybrid projects at 2.5 GW, manufacturing at 1.9 GW, large-scale solar at 1.2 GW, and rooftop solar at 51.2 MW.",
